 "notes": [
  "Bed capacity x occupancy x revenue per occupied bed does NOT give the revenue: for FY25 the presentation's 1,605 beds, 61% and Rs 30,829 give Rs 11,017 million against Rs 8,805 million reported. Occupancy is counted on fewer beds than the capacity printed, and that count is not printed.",
  "So for the past the block runs backwards: revenue, occupancy and revenue per occupied bed are typed, and the beds in use are worked out (revenue / days / occupancy / price). The forecast then runs forwards from that count.",
  "Revenue per occupied bed is all hospital revenue (outpatients and pharmacy included) over occupied bed days, so no second revenue line is needed here.",
  "A first-quarter filing has no balance sheet and no cash flow. The model starts from the 31 March 2026 balance sheet, which is from a secondary source until the user saves the FY26 filing.",
  "Beds in use at the end of June 2026 is not printed anywhere; the quarter's average stands in for it."
 ],
